LOCKED IDEA
===========

  UNSEEN — a phone that shows you motion your eyes can't resolve.

Point it at a hand and watch a pulse appear. Point it at a fan and see the
bearing that's about to fail. Point it at the ceiling lights and read the
flicker frequency nobody knew was there.

Full plan:  docs/07-instruments.md
Team page:  https://claude.ai/artifact/9XfYmYj56wfpLVB24GecEj


THE FIVE-QUESTION CHECK  (docs/04 §4)
-------------------------------------
  [x] 1. Usable in under 10 seconds, no account?        open link, point camera
  [x] 2. Works on a judge's own phone?                  any phone with a camera
  [x] 3. Understandable in under 90 seconds?            "point it at your hand"
  [x] 4. Can the room see something happen?             pulse on the projector
  [x] 5. If the API dies mid-demo, does it keep working? yes - the instrument is
         local; Claude only interprets, and falls back to cached text


BUILD ORDER  (ship the floor first)
-----------------------------------
  1. Capture -> downscale -> per-pixel temporal bandpass -> amplify  [G1]
  2. Colour mode: a visible pulse on a real hand                     [G2]  <- shippable
  3. Flicker mode: rolling shutter -> FFT -> Hz + modulation depth   [G3]
  4. Claude interpretation layer + caps + kill switch                [G3]
  5. Motion mode  (CUTTABLE - drop it if noisy at 02:00)             [G3]


